{"name":"Royal Pretender","hex":"#a063a1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"royal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to a monarch or his (or her) family.","Having the air or demeanour of a monarch; illustrious; magnanimous; of more than common size or excellence."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A royal person; a member of a royal family.","A standard size of printing paper, measuring 25 by 20 inches."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royal"},{"term":"pretender","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who intends or purposes.","One who puts forth a claim, or who aspires to or aims at something; a claimant, candidate, or aspirant; now, one who makes baseless pretensions.\n\n One who aspires to the hand of a woman in marriage; a suitor, a wooer.\n\nA claimant to a throne or the office of a ruler; originally in a neutral sense, but now always applied to a claimant who is held to have no just title."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To tender (a bid, etc.) in advance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pretender"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pretender","blocks":[{"text":"A pretender is someone who claims to be the rightful ruler of a country although not recognized as such by the current government. The term may often be used to either refer to a descendant of a deposed monarchy or a claim that is not legitimate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/James_Francis_Edward_Stuart_c._1703_attributed_to_Alexis_Simon_Belle.jpg/330px-James_Francis_Edward_Stuart_c._1703_attributed_to_Alexis_Simon_Belle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pretender"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Karl_Emich_of_Leiningen_photo7.jpg/500px-Karl_Emich_of_Leiningen_photo7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"h